    "durationMs": 378150,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete. I built the URL shortener with axum 0.8.4 + sqlx (PostgreSQL) and verified it end-to-end.\n\n**What's in place:**\n- `src/main.rs` — full API: `POST /links` (generated or custom codes, 409 on duplicates), `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` (manual 302 + atomic `UPDATE ... clicks + 1 RETURNING`, since axum's `Redirect::temporary` emits 307), `GET /links` (ascending creation order via auto-increment id). Validation via the `url` crate: absolute http/https with host required; codes 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`; malformed JSON/invalid url/invalid code all → 422 `{\"error\": ...}`.\n- `migrations/0001_create_links.sql` — `links` table; applied at startup via `sqlx::migrate!` (binary supports a `migrate` subcommand so `start.sh` applies migrations before serving).\n- `start.sh` (executable) — runs `migrate`, then `exec`s the server in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; rebuilds only if the prebuilt release binary is missing. `DATABASE_URL` comes from the environment, nothing hard-coded.\n- `README.md` — includes the required \"Starting the server\" section.\n\n**Verification:** a 25-check curl suite passed clean (creation, duplicates, all 422/404/409 paths, 302 `Location` exactness, click incrementing once per request, listing order). I then killed the server, re-ran `sh start.sh`, and confirmed links and click counts survived the restart. The test server is stopped and port 8000 is free."
  }
